AGPL-3.0-or-later; LICENSE holds the license text.

Modified from the upstream files above, 2026-11-22: kept only the
inference path of the SM98 instant-only model with f32 state and scalar
kernels; removed the Anki collection, protobuf, SQLite state cache, Rayon,
SIMD kernels, state quantization, curves, intervals and forecasts; added
the %seer revlog mapping (src/seer.rs) and the WebAssembly ABI
(src/abi.rs).

Corresponding Source. tools/build-rwkv-artifact builds engine.wasm and
writes, beside it, this NOTICE, LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES (the licenses
of the crates compiled into engine.wasm, from Cargo.lock) and
rwkv-engine-source.tar, the Corresponding Source of that engine.wasm: this
crate's manifest, lock file, toolchain pin, src/, LICENSE and notices, and
the build script itself. Unpack the tar and run tools/build-rwkv-artifact
to rebuild engine.wasm byte for byte with the pinned toolchain. Whoever
conveys engine.wasm must offer that tar from the same place.

The model weights are not part of this crate or its repository. The build
fetches qt/aqt/rwkv_inference/sm98/weights.int8.bin from the commit above
(SHA-256 b2f335bd712b9d602150201de41ab5a0f0a4c291644705e2aa1ed2a1bf1592c3);
the fork states no license for them. The same bytes are
rwkv-small-instant-only/weights.int8.bin in the SM98 release of

  https://github.com/JSchoreels/anki-rwkv/releases/tag/rwkv-family-2026-11-13

whose WEIGHTS-NOTICE.md, copied unchanged to WEIGHTS-NOTICE.md here, says
the weights are not covered by the MIT License, that whether they may be
redistributed is an open question upstream, and that until it is settled
they are for personal and research use only and the dataset's owners should
be asked before the weights are shipped in an application. Serving
weights.bin to browsers, from any host including your own ship, is
redistribution.
